# Copy this file to .env before running Terraform or the deploy.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This file is for OPERATOR tooling — Terraform and wrangler. The
# application itself reads almost nothing from here: on Workers it gets
# its database and its bucket as bindings, and its one secret from
# `wrangler secret put`. See apps/web/.dev.vars.example for that.

# The single Cloudflare API token, used by Terraform (via infra/tf) and
# by wrangler (via apps/web/cf).
#
# Five permissions are required:
#
#   Account · Workers R2 Storage · Edit
#   Account · D1 · Edit
#   Account · Workers Scripts · Edit
#   Zone    · DNS · Edit
#   Zone    · Single Redirect · Edit
#
# Set them in ONE edit. Editing a Cloudflare token REPLACES its
# permission list rather than adding to it, so granting one can silently
# revoke another. Check all five at once with:
#
#   ./infra/check-token
#
# A token short of any of them fails partway through a terraform apply
# or a deploy rather than up front.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Optional: wrangler can usually infer the account from the token, but
# an account with more than one membership needs it stated.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Send-to-Kindle, over Resend.
#
# Putting the key here does NOT switch the feature on. The application
# reads the Worker environment, not this file — this one is for
# Terraform and wrangler. The same value has to reach two other places:
#
#   apps/web/.dev.vars                       for `wrangler dev`
#   ./cf npx wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY   for production
#
# Keeping it here as well is still worth doing: it is the copy operator
# tooling can read, and both files are git-ignored.
#
# Use a restricted "sending access" key. Nothing in NobleSee manages
# domains or reads mail, so a full-access key grants reach nothing needs.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# --- LLM, for the AI correction stage ---
# Read by the Worker at runtime, so it must ALSO exist as a Worker
# secret — this file is only for local tooling:
#
#   wrangler secret put XAI_API_KEY
#
# This was the converter container's key until 2026-08-26. The container
# is gone and the correction stage runs in the Worker (CLAUDE.md section
# 13), so the key moved with the code. Unset, correction jobs fail with
# a clear message; nothing else in the pipeline is affected.
#
# Defaults to xAI with the cheap non-reasoning text model: correction is
# a narrow task over short inputs, and reasoning tokens are billed as
# output at twice the input rate.
#
# To use a self-hosted vLLM endpoint instead, which needs no key:
#   LLM_PROVIDER=vllm
#   VLLM_BASE_URL=http://10.211.51.231:8000/v1
XAI_API_KEY=

# --- Google sign-in ---
# Both are read by the Worker at runtime, so they must ALSO exist as
# Worker secrets — `.env` is only for local tooling:
#
#   cd apps/web
#   ./cf npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID
#   ./cf npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET
#
# and in apps/web/.dev.vars for `wrangler dev`.
#
# Both redirect URIs must be registered on the client in the Google
# Cloud Console, exactly, including scheme and port:
#
#   https://noblesee.com/auth/google/callback
#   http://localhost:8787/auth/google/callback
#
# The button only renders when both variables are present, so an
# installation without them shows an ordinary password-only sign-in page
# rather than a broken button.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
